  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Saturday)\nIssued at 1227 AM CDT Sun Aug 16 2026\n\nModel agreement continues to trend towards the current upper-level\nhigh retrograding back west during the course of next week. This\nretrograde will eventually see said high back over the Panhandles\nresulting in a return of the more widespread triple-digit\ntemperatures for Tuesday alongside the potential need for another\nround of heat related products. Unfortunately this return of high\npressure will see our chances of storms drop off for the day as\nwell. However, present GFS and ECMWF runs have finally gotten into\nbetter agreement on the supposed trough digging south sometime\nWednesday into Thursday. Currently these runs have see the main\naxis of the trough further east then what the GFS was initially\ntrying to do, which will keep keep us out of the main activity\npush from the trough unfortunately. However, this position does\nopen the Panhandles to some very good northwesterly upper-level\nflow, which will be beneficial in seeing storms push off the\nmountains to our west and into our area once again. Present\nensembles have also picked up on the idea with current NBM now\ngiving us a 10 to 20 percent chance of seeing precipitation in our\nwest and north clear into Friday evening. However, given that this\nhigh have been staying very potent in most of the model runs\nconfidence in these chances holding out are not too high. For now,\nlook for temperatures in the upper 90s to triple-digits to be the\nnorm for the week.",
